# XCU mailx
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# mailx in Receive Mode reading a secondary mailbox with -f and commands
# from standard input; the prompt is turned off with set noprompt and echo
# lines with distinctive markers split the output into sections. Message
# text uses unique tokens so printing is checked by presence and absence
# only; header summary layouts, size units and message print layouts beyond
# the required pieces are not examined. Send Mode, the system mailbox and
# the interactive input mode need a mail transfer agent or a terminal and
# are recorded as untestable.

assertion  XCU.mailx.001
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       print and type (with their abbreviations) write the named message
           to standard output without the other messages, and Print and Type
           write it with all of its header fields.
test       t/001-print-type.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.002
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       A message list can be a number, a range n-m, several numbers, *
           for all, $ for the last, ^ for the first, + and - for the next
           and previous message, /string for a Subject match ignoring case,
           or an address.
test       t/002-message-lists.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.003
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       Deleted messages are not shown by later commands and are removed
           from the file when mailx quits (by quit or end-of-file) but not
           by exit; undelete restores them; delete with no list deletes the
           current message.
test       t/003-delete-and-quit.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.004
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#OUTPUT FILES
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       save and copy append the messages with their headers in the
           mailbox file format, creating the file, with no file operand save
           goes to the mbox, and write puts the message without its header
           into the file.
test       t/004-save-write-copy.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.005
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       from and headers write one summary line per message that is not
           deleted, the current message line begins with >, -H writes only
           the summary and exits, and -N leaves out the initial summary.
test       t/005-header-summary.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.006
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       The current message starts as the first message, = writes its
           number, a command with a list leaves the highest numbered message
           of the list current, and next prints the current message if it
           has not been shown, then each following message in turn.
test       t/006-current-and-next.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.007
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#OPERANDS
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       file switches to another mailbox file, # names the previous file,
           + names a file in the folder directory, file with no argument
           says which mailbox is open, -f with no operand reads the mbox,
           and -i is accepted.
test       t/007-change-file.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.008
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       top writes only the first few lines of a message, as many as the
           toplines variable says (default 5), so a long message is cut
           short and a large toplines value shows all of it.
test       t/008-top.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.009
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       echo writes its strings as the echo utility does (abbreviations
           accepted, quotes keep spacing), a # line is ignored, source runs
           commands from a file, ! runs a shell command, and set defines a
           variable that set lists and unset removes.
test       t/009-echo-set-source.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.010
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       pipe and | give the listed messages to a shell command as its
           standard input; with no arguments the current message goes to the
           command held in the cmd variable.
test       t/010-pipe.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.011
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       ignore (and discard) hide the named header fields, ignoring case,
           when messages are written with print, Print overrides that, a
           command without names lists the hidden names, and retain shows
           only the named fields.
test       t/011-header-field-filters.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.012
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       alias and group record the addresses of a name, alias with a name
           lists it, alias with no arguments lists all, unalias removes one,
           and alternates stores and lists alternative addresses.
test       t/012-aliases.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.013
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       Naming a file with -f that cannot be read gives a non-zero exit
           status.
test       t/013-missing-file.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.014
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Send Mode
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#ASYNCHRONOUS EVENTS
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Command Escapes in mailx
class      untestable
since      1992
says       Send Mode delivers standard input as a message with -E and -s, -e
           and -u examine a system mailbox, hold, preserve, mbox and touch
           act on the system mailbox, and reply, mail, followup and the
           tilde escapes compose messages in input mode.
reason     Delivery needs a mail transfer agent and recipients, the system
           mailbox has an unspecified location and need not be a file, and
           input mode is defined for a terminal; none of these can be set up
           or inspected portably from a script.

assertion  XCU.mailx.015
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       Command arguments can be quoted with paired double or single quotes,
           which keep white space and dollar signs literally and leave the other
           quote kind literal; a backslash outside quotes is dropped and the next
           character stays literal; a backslash at the end of a line joins the
           next line to the command.
test       t/015-quoting.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.016
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      2024
says       A file name starting with an unquoted + is placed in the folder
           directory (a relative folder name is taken from HOME), is left alone
           when folder is unset, shell word expansion applies to file names, and
           quoted characters stay literal.
test       t/016-filenames.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.017
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       cd and chdir change the directory used for relative file names, and
           with no argument go to HOME.
test       t/017-cd.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.018
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       The file command takes & for the current mbox, the file named by MBOX.
test       t/018-file-mbox.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.019
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       Deleted messages are ignored by message lists and shown by no command
           but undelete; undelete can name them with /string, :d or, with no
           list, the next deleted message after the current one else the last one
           before it; after a delete the current message is the first remaining
           one after the deleted ones, else the one before.
test       t/019-deleted-state.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.020
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       A message written by print or top is in state read, and :r in a
           message list selects the read messages.
test       t/020-read-state.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.021
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       When mailx quits, read messages of a secondary mailbox stay in that
           file and are not moved to the mbox.
test       t/021-quit-keeps-read.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.022
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       A command line with no command is taken as next.
test       t/022-empty-command.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.023
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       set name, set name= and set name=string define variables that set
           lists (a quoted value keeps its blanks), set noname erases a variable
           like unset, and unset takes several names.
test       t/023-set-forms.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.024
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       The command mode prompt is written to standard output and is by
           default "? "; prompt=string changes it, and a null prompt or noprompt
           turns it off.
test       t/024-prompt.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.025
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Start-Up in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       The commands in the start-up file named by MAILRC are executed at
           start-up and a blank line in it is ignored.
test       t/025-startup-file.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.026
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      conditional
when       UP
since      2024
says       The ! command and the pipe command run their command through the
           program named by SHELL, called with exactly the three arguments -c, --
           and the command.
test       t/026-shell-invocation.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.027
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       By default pipe adds nothing between messages; with page set it
           inserts a form-feed after each message it sends to the command.
test       t/027-pipe-page.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.028
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       With autoprint set, delete writes the current message and undelete the
           last message restored (both leaving the written message in state
           read); by default neither writes; dp and dt write the message that
           becomes current only when it follows the deleted ones, ignore
           autoprint, and mark it read.
test       t/028-autoprint-dp.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.029
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       if r runs the following commands in Receive Mode and if s does not;
           else reverses that, and endif or en ends the block.
test       t/029-if-else.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.030
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       help and ? write a summary of commands and list writes the names of
           the available commands, all to standard output.
test       t/030-help-list.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.031
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       With screen set to 1, headers n writes only the page holding message n
           and makes it current, headers alone does not change the current
           message, and z, z+ and z- scroll the header display by one page.
test       t/031-headers-z.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.032
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       edit and visual put each named message in a temporary file and run the
           program named by EDITOR or VISUAL on it in turn, without changing the
           messages in the mailbox.
test       t/032-edit-visual.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.033
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       folders writes the names of the files in the folder directory using
           the command named by LISTER, or ls when LISTER is null.
test       t/033-folders.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.034
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       size writes the size in bytes of a message: two messages whose headers
           have the same length and whose bodies differ by 96 bytes differ by 96
           in size.
test       t/034-size.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.035
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      2024
says       When standard output is a terminal and crt is set below the number of
           lines in a message the message is written through the command named by
           PAGER; by default (no crt) or with a larger crt it is written
           directly.
test       t/035-crt-pager.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.036
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       Save and Copy write the messages, with all their header fields even if
           some are ignored for display, to a file named for the author of the
           first message with the network address removed.
test       t/036-save-author.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.037
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       When both retain and ignore are given, only the retained fields are
           shown, whichever came first.
test       t/037-retain-over-ignore.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.038
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Commands in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      2024
says       By default an exclamation mark in a ! command is literal; with bang
           set each unescaped one is replaced by the previous ! command.
test       t/038-bang.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.039
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       By default an address in a message list selects only messages from
           exactly that address; with allnet set, network names with the same
           login name match.
test       t/039-allnet.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.040
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       The header summary is written on entering Receive Mode by default, and
           not when header is unset.
test       t/040-header-variable.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.041
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       Options can be grouped in one argument and -- ends the options before
           the file operand.
test       t/041-option-syntax.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.042
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       With MAILRC unset the start-up file is .mailrc in HOME, and with MBOX
           unset the mbox is the file mbox in HOME.
test       t/042-default-files.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.043
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       When every message of a secondary mailbox has been deleted, quitting
           removes the file by default and truncates it to zero length when keep
           is set.
test       t/043-keep.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.044
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       By default the header summary line shows the author of a message; with
           showto set, a message sent by the invoking user shows the To field
           instead.
test       t/044-showto.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.045
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       On entering Receive Mode mailx writes an opening message unless quiet
           is set.
test       t/045-quiet.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.046
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       In a message list, a period stands for the current message.
test       t/046-dot-message.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.047
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Start-Up in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       An error in the start-up file, such as an unknown command or a command
           invalid there like !, either ends mailx with a diagnostic and a non-
           zero status or lets it continue after a diagnostic while ignoring the
           rest of the file; an invalid command is not carried out.
test       t/047-startup-errors.sh

assertion  XCU.mailx.048
anchor     utilities/mailx.html#Internal Variables in mailx
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       At start-up the variables whose default is no... are not defined and
           the ones whose default is set (header, save, asksub) are, as set
           shows.
test       t/048-default-variables.sh
